## Derived source

Two source files were written from Apache-2.0 examples in the gpui crate of
the Zed editor (https://github.com/zed-industries/zed, tag v1.6.3,
crates/gpui), and both have been modified. The upstream distribution carries
no NOTICE file of its own.

    ui/components/src/text_input.rs   from examples/input.rs
    ui/shell/src/chrome.rs            from examples/window_shadow.rs

Apache License 2.0: LICENSES/gpui.txt

The URL pattern in terminal/src/display/mod.rs is alacritty's own hint regex,
taken as it stands from alacritty/src/config/ui_config.rs
(https://github.com/alacritty/alacritty, tag v0.17.0). Alacritty carries no
NOTICE file of its own.

Apache License 2.0: LICENSES/alacritty.txt

## Patched dependency source

A patch carries the lines it replaces and those around them, so a patch under
patches/ that reshapes more than a line or two both copies and modifies the
source it applies to.

Eclipse Layout Kernel, Rust port 0.11.0+rs.2 — Eclipse Public License 2.0
    Content of the Eclipse Layout Kernel project, ported to Rust by
    openedges. The content is the property of its respective authors or their
    employers; Eclipse Layout Kernel is a trademark of the Eclipse Foundation.
    https://projects.eclipse.org/projects/modeling.elk
    https://github.com/openedges/elk-rs
    patches/elk-rs-reentrant-external-port-lock.patch
    LICENSES/elk-rs.txt

That patch carries some fifty lines of Eclipse Public License 2.0 source and
rewrites them, so the patch is itself available under that licence.

The patches against gpui_linux carry Apache-2.0 lines from the same Zed tree
the derived files above come from, under the terms in LICENSES/gpui.txt. The
xkbcommon patch carries a module declaration, a cfg attribute and six lines
around them — too little to attribute.

## Colour values

The palette in ui/theme/themes/one.json is data, not code, and its own terms
sit beside it in ui/theme/themes/LICENSE.

The Oklab conversion in ui/theme/src/lib.rs uses the reference constants Björn
Ottosson publishes with "A perceptual color space for image processing"
(https://bottosson.github.io/posts/oklab/). They are cited at the point they
are used; the entry is here to record where they came from.

## Dependencies

Crates, Bazel modules and toolchains that bviz builds against are pinned in
MODULE.bazel and Cargo.lock and carry their own terms; they are not restated
here.
